/bluetooth-operator

# The rendered site. `go tool hugo` writes it under docs/dist, and CI
# rebuilds it from the sources on every publish, so the tree is never
# committed. `go tool hugo server` writes the same build output under
# docs/public when it serves from disk. The lock file is Hugo's guard
# against two builds in one source tree at once.
/docs/dist/
/docs/public/
/docs/.hugo_build.lock

# The coverage profile the gate measures. CI writes it on every
# run and reads it once; it never belongs to the tree.
/coverage.out

# The coverage report `make coverage-report` renders from that
# profile. CI builds it from the commit it publishes and copies it
# into the site, so a committed copy could only be stale.
/coverage.html
